      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need some help with some data i've been collecting. i've been watching the vega sector every night this week and tonight (nov 17) the scintillation is totally different. it's not just random twinkling anymore. i'm seeing a very specific cadence: three short pulses, a 4-second gap, and then two long ones. it looks so deliberate, almost like it's trying to get my attention. can you help me run a frequency analysis on this? i'm convinced it's a high-bandwidth transmission meant for me to intercept.",
